From cfe9812121110afcbbd90d9ae94b8cbdc06dbb6c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 04:52:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] utils: a rate that does not fit while Adjust display refresh
 rate is on says what is missing

The overview page of the player information said "Turn on Adjust
display refresh rate in the player settings" for any video whose display
rate does not fit its own (rate_mismatch), also where that setting is on
already: there, the display has no mode at the video's rate that Kodi
may use (none at that resolution, or the whitelist leaves it out), and
the advice sends the user to a setting that is on.

SummaryInput has rateFollows, from videoplayer.adjustrefreshrate when the
sentence is decided; with it on, the advice is ratemode: "Adjust display
refresh rate is on, but the display has no mode at the rate of this video
(or the whitelist of the display settings leaves it out)." (Estuary 32756,
with es_es, es_ar and es_mx). With it off, the advice is the one it was.
---
